        "text": "Investors and traders perform analysis before risking their money. The analysis frameworks can be broken down broadly into two fundamental analysis and technical analysis. Fundamental analysis tries to identify an asset's intrinsic value. This is achieved by looking at economic and financial factors. In an attempt to find the fair value of an asset, you may look at macroeconomic factors like the global economy or an industry state. Microeconomic factors can also be important if you're investing in a business or an asset related to a business. The end goal is to establish whether an investment is undervalued or overvalued by the market price.",
